WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.813
Python gives us more than one way

00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:04.605
to import code The first style is

00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:08.171
to import the entire module For example

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:11.303
import math When we use this style

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.395
we usually write the module name before

00:00:13.408 --> 00:00:15.408
the function such as math dot square

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.171
root The second style is to use

00:00:18.197 --> 00:00:21.329
an alias An alias gives a module

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:25.224
a shorter name For example import statistics

00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:28.276
as stats After that we can write

00:00:28.303 --> 00:00:30.539
stats dot mean instead of statistics dot

00:00:30.553 --> 00:00:34.118
mean Aliases are especially common in data

00:00:34.132 --> 00:00:37.276
analytics Later in the course you will

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.710
often see NumPy imported as N P

00:00:39.737 --> 00:00:42.763
and Pandas imported as P D These

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:45.789
aliases are widely recognized by Python users

00:00:46.711 --> 00:00:48.895
The third style is a selective import

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:52.500
For example from math import square root

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:57.408
This imports one specific function directly After

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.434
that we can call square root without

00:00:59.447 --> 00:01:02.316
writing the module name first There is

00:01:02.342 --> 00:01:04.355
no single import style that is always

00:01:04.382 --> 00:01:08.921
best The choice depends on readability If

00:01:08.947 --> 00:01:10.645
you need several tools from the same

00:01:10.671 --> 00:01:13.184
module importing the whole module is often

00:01:13.197 --> 00:01:16.197
clear If a short alias is standard

00:01:16.224 --> 00:01:18.329
and easy to recognize an alias can

00:01:18.355 --> 00:01:20.934
make the code easier to read If

00:01:20.961 --> 00:01:23.105
you only need one specific function a

00:01:23.132 --> 00:01:26.750
selective import can be convenient The important

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:28.987
rule is to keep the code understandable

00:01:29.921 --> 00:01:32.329
Do not create unusual aliases just to

00:01:32.355 --> 00:01:35.447
save a few characters Shorter code is

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.263
not automatically better code
